{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdRE84QNRtL4VtLoetPyE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-305 is complete. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## What the defect was\n\n119-CRITIQUE's **T1 (MAJOR)**: SR-054's core reading task \"find the next work\" had **no path** on the dashboard. With zero `active` rows nothing marked \"you are here\", the Process tab's resume loop is a static diagram, and the only route to a queued item was `When → double-click a phase → double-click a workstream → scan for a queued node` — the anchor's own bad case.\n\n## The fix\n\nAdded a named **\"Next work\"** surface to the landing hero (`PROJECT_STATE.html`), so the task costs **zero tab switches**:\n\n- `gen_trajectory.py` — new `_next_work_html(root)` helper renders the dependency-ready WIs from **`schedule.frontier`** (the same IF-071 derivation already projected into `status.md`), in scheduler build order, **named**. Ready WIs first; the next **waiting** WIs follow, each annotated with its **blocking predecessor** (`after WI-X`) — literally \"the ready/queued WIs, named, with their blocking predecessor.\" A drained registry says \"All work items are done\" rather than rendering empty.\n- Styling reuses the `.card` box + declared U1 type scale + theme-only colours (so U1/U2 uniformity stay clean); deterministic (no clocks) so `--check` stays byte-stable; **OPTIONAL** exactly like `_frontier_lines` — a scaffold without `schedule.py` renders nothing.\n- Verified end-to-end against the real registry: shows WI-305/306/307/308/314 ready + WI-315 \"after WI-305\".\n\n## Bar\n\n- **Full suite green: 1559 passed, 8 skipped.** Three new tests cover the ready-frontier / blocking-predecessor / drained states.\n- `test_module_size_ratchet.py`: reviewed baseline bump `5007 → 5112` with a reasoned entry.\n- Pre-commit floor **all PASS** (freshness, format, privacy). Committed as **`54cf50f`** with the required `WI:/Train:/Base:` trailers.\n\n## Two things flagged (not fixed — out of scope)\n\n1. **Verification=Critique**: this changes a render surface, so it needs a fresh family-heterogeneous critique to clear the perceptual-stale gate (the `trajectory` step WARNs this). A worker can't self-issue one — flagged for the integrator/owner critique flow.\n2. **Pre-existing lint (unrelated)**: `tests/test_trace.py:1256,1403` use `pytest.skip` without importing `pytest` (ruff F821) — present on the base `a67ceb9`, in the G3-only lint step. Left untouched per the \"don't fix unrelated code\" agreement.\n\nNote: `PROJECT_STATE.html` was regenerated to pass the pre-commit freshness floor (established train-worktree practice); the integrator re-regenerates it on the composed tree via the `[generated]` auto-resolve."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":340,"cache_read_input_tokens":211989,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":340},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d821d632-5be2-40cf-bedf-e60f574faeaf","uuid":"122411f4-a131-4e4c-9ba6-b2cccf3dfe1a","request_id":"req_011CdRE82wZJ58SRob664em4"}
